  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted (config_019, acc 0.706) is the best configuration, with the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000) providing the largest single gain (+0.071). The one untested design dimension in this top-performing setup is aggregation: in RNA-only experiments avgpool beat transformer (0.591 vs 0.519), but that comparison used the simpler pca_n2000 encoder. With scvi_n200's richer per-profile representations, a transformer aggregator could potentially capture inter-profile interactions that a simple mean discards. config_031 changes only aggregation (avgpool→transformer) relative to config_019, isolating this single factor. If it matches or beats 0.706, it opens a new optimization axis; if it underperforms, it confirms avgpool is robust across encoder quality and redirects effort toward other levers. Under a tight budget, this single-variable test from the current best is the highest-information next step."
}

